	(text "Q1 SOA RELEASE GATE\nProve IPB020N10N5LF at the hot corner: approximately 66 W inferred maximum power limit and 66.5 ms maximum TIMER interval.\nDo not substitute Q1 using RDS(on) alone. Validate current/power limits and startup on hardware."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 292.1 94 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "201e33b9-1b46-40b6-ad34-825ea71630b7")
	)
	(text "R17/R18 are Kelvin sense traces from the R1 pads. U4 VBUS intentionally measures after Q1."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 195.58 99.06 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.05 1.05)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "2761a200-8095-4141-9bac-9b039feac66d")
	)
	(text "LM5163 Type-3 ripple injection; nominal 3.3 V / ~300 kHz. Keep SW/BST/ripple loop compact during PCB layout."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 99.06 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.05 1.05)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "365943f5-90b5-4f64-84c4-da6710c6ab21")
	)
	(text "RELEASE BLOCKER - CONNECTOR POLARITY\nCurrent carrier assumption: J1 pin 1 = VIN_RAW, pin 2 = GND, pin 3 = SDA, pin 4 = SCL.\nBackplane-prototype presently shows the power pins oppositely. Confirm physical mated contacts and drawing viewpoints,\nthen make symbol pins, footprint pads, net assignments, and notes consistent in every carrier/backplane project before fabrication."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 292.1 18 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "5c608385-3f45-4bf9-9c37-b37415e5178a")
	)
	(text "Default OFF: R8/R9 drive Q2 on unless PA1 drives Q3. LMX5069 auto-retries; STM32 observes PD_PGOOD and may remove PD_ENABLE."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 187.96 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.05 1.05)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "5d8ba6ad-1cf2-4950-9386-d7c236c12871")
	)
